# HeyEddi always-on

The working agreement for **every Agent chat** in this project. Skills hold the playbooks and scripts; where a skill disagrees with this file, this file wins.

## Checklist

1. **Autonomy**: A request to build, fix, or change something approves the whole pipeline. Run it to completion on a feature branch (worktree when `git.worktrees` is true); the user decides at merge. Never end the turn for status, plan confirmation, picking between reasonable options, cost, or scan findings. Missing info: read `.heyeddi/` and the repo, take the documented default, record it, keep going. One final summary: Cost (only when over budget), Done, Tests, Assumptions, Needs you, Next. Detail: `@heyeddi` `reference/autonomy.md`.
2. **Router / `.heyeddi/`**: Session start or ambiguous task: `@heyeddi`. Keep `.heyeddi/skills-index` current; follow `.heyeddi/docs/intake/skill-routing.json` when present. Run the next pipeline skill yourself while it is part of the request. Do not re-scaffold workflow every message.
3. **Setup**: Before the first git action of a session: `@heyeddi-setup` `verify_setup --check`. If incomplete, run `write_setup.py --defaults` (no questions) and keep working.
4. **Permissions**: Before commit, push, PR, merge, release, or any command that touches dev / staging / prod: `@heyeddi-local-first` `check_permission.py --command "<cmd>" --check`. Exit 0: run it, no question. Exit 2: ask once, batched, keep working meanwhile, rerun with `--approved` on a yes. Exit 1: never run it; hand that step to the user or the pipeline and finish the rest. Policy: `agent.preset` in `.heyeddi/stack.json` (default `balanced`).
5. **Tests**: Test first, at the layers the change can break: unit for logic, integration for API / DB / rules / auth boundaries, component or Playwright (local app, test login) for UI flows. A bug starts with a failing test at the lowest layer that reproduces it. Not every layer every time; say which ran and which you skipped and why. Hosted environments (test, staging, production): look and navigate only. No destructive action. Detail: `@heyeddi` `reference/testing.md`.
6. **Engineering**: Before feature code: `@engineering-excellence` plan gate. After edits: `audit_engineering --check` (errors fail; warns advisory).
7. **Cost**: After edits: `estimate_change_cost`. It never stops the work. State $/month in the plan when it names a cost driver. Over budget: keep the change on the branch and lead the final summary with the range, top drivers, and the cheaper option. `@pre-merge-gate` blocks the merge until the user approves.
8. **Browser platform (frontend and design)**: Frontend and design skills load `@heyeddi` `reference/browser-platform.md`. On existing UI, run Modern Web Guidance `legacy-scan` on the files you touch, verify the hits, and fix them. Quasar, PrimeVue Aura, and Aura tokens stay the component source. Playwright is the screenshot and signed-in test tool. Fresh Chrome profile, localhost only.
9. **Prose and links**: Any prose you author (chat, docs, UI, PRs, books): follow `PROSE_ANTI_SLOP`. Run `verify_prose --check` on touched surfaces; add `--glob` for other paths. Every PR, issue, commit, CI run, or deploy you mention gets its full URL as a link, for example `[#64](https://github.com/org/repo/pull/64)`; `gh pr view <n> --json url -q .url` returns it. A bare `#64` is never enough.
10. **Ship**: Before merge-ready claims: `@pre-merge-gate --signoff` (exit 0 required).

## On demand (not every chat)

`@heyeddi-intake`, `@heyeddi-product`, `@taste-penpot`, `@heyeddi-design`, visual/UX auditors, `@heyeddi-pr-review`, `@heyeddi-pr-respond`, scaffolders / handoff.

